+# Decision: the lab is the central Scope, and the processes it keeps
+
+Decided by Justin on 2026-10-04, in an interview that afternoon. Copied from `STATE.md` as it stood at 2026-10-04 17:31,
+which held the only copy in this Scope; `STATE.md` is overwritten at each verified event. Recording these is not
+deciding them again. The wording is the summary that `STATE.md` recorded, kept as it was written there.
+
+## Decided
+
+- **The lab is the central Scope** for project management, core issue tracking, code quality and security. Astra is to
+  say what else it should cover.
+- **Where issues live:** a Scope's issues stay in its own repository, on one central map; a `core` label marks a Scope
+  issue that needs ORC's core changed. Later, Scopes may track their own business logic elsewhere.
+- **The processes kept, all of them:**
+  - map and label check;
+  - tests on every PR (#144);
+  - the security-review and package-API checks;
+  - daily diary;
+  - weekly adversarial review;
+  - entropy guard at session end;
+  - FRICTION into rules, monthly (#60);
+  - branch and worktree cleanup (#70);
+  - `/tmp` cleanup (#182).
+- **ORC scheduling (#166) is built first,** and the scheduled ones run through it.
+- **Astra runs entropy-guard's assessment on ORC and the lab together.** Justin is shaping the brief before it runs.
+
+Recorded on the same day in `STATE.md`, outside the interview list:
+
+- **MS is paused** (Justin, 4 Oct): browser-stack work that touches it (#118, #52, MS #52) waits.
+
+## Still open on 4 October
+
+- **Labels:** the type-label proposal waits on Astra's revisions (`reports/2026-10-04-labels-review-astra.md`).
+- **Tests on every PR (#144):** kept as a process; whether it runs in GitHub Actions or a pre-push hook is Justin's
+  choice, still open.
+
+## Proposed, awaiting Justin
+
+- `scope.yaml`'s `purpose` still describes the lab as the Scope for developing and operating ORC and its agents, and
+  three lists name the repositories the lab oversees (`scope.yaml`, `tools/collect.mjs` and the map). The entropy
+  assessment of 2026-10-07 proposes widening `purpose` to the role decided above and naming those repositories in one
+  place. Not applied: `scope.yaml` follows the generic Scope model in `~/pro/scope/docs/MODEL.md`, which the assessment
+  did not read. (`SCOPE.md` was corrected from this decision directly.)
